{"repo": {"timestamp": 1795867645005, "version": 30000, "name": "Caracole", "icon": "icon.png", "address": "https://danielhp95.github.io/caracole/fdroid/repo", "description": "Multi-site and multi-instrument tablature indexer with support for offline reads, songbook exporting and many other features."}, "requests": {"install": [], "uninstall": []}, "apps": [{"antiFeatures": ["NonFreeNet"], "authorName": "Daniel Hernandez", "categories": ["Multimedia", "Reading"], "suggestedVersionCode": "5", "description": "caracole keeps a copy of your caracole library on the phone and runs caracole\nthere, so it works with the computer off.\n\n* Your library, offline: the library page, every sheet with all its tools\n  (key, capo, chord diagrams, harmony, pinyin, strum), kept versions,\n  harmonica tabs and songbooks.\n* Search and fetch from the phone: the computer's site indexes come with a\n  sync, so the phone's search finds songs on the sites offline.\n* Sync with your computer: the two libraries each take what the other\n  changed; where both changed a song, you pick which to keep.\n* Guitar Pro on the phone: a file drawn as score and tab and played.\n* Share to caracole: share a song from a music app to find it or fetch it.\n* Chords from audio: give it a song's audio file and it works out the\n  chords and the beats on the phone, under the lyrics it finds, with no\n  computer. It needs Android 13, an arm64 phone and 6 GB of memory, and\n  downloads its models once, at a tap (about 55 MB, from caracole's GitHub\n  release and the chord model's authors' repository).\n* A sheet from a YouTube video: paste or share a video and the phone takes\n  its audio with its own yt-dlp and makes the song's sheet from it. It also\n  does so by itself, on Wi-Fi, for a song no sheet site has (a setting turns\n  that off). Taking audio from YouTube goes against YouTube's terms. It needs\n  the chord models and an arm64 phone.\n\nIt needs a computer running caracole serve to sync from:\nhttps